{
  "id": "parachicos_chiapa_de_corzo",
  "name": "Parachicos (Chiapa de Corzo January fiesta music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "In the Fiesta Grande de Enero of Chiapa de Corzo, Chiapas, held each January for the Lord of Esquipulas, San Antonio Abad and San Sebastián, masked parachico dancers parade through the town led by the patrón, who carries a guitar and a whip and plays a cane flute with one or two drummers, while the dancers answer his calls with shouts and shake rattles called chinchines. UNESCO inscribed the parachicos of the January feast on its Representative List in 2010. A generic flute card stands in for the patrón's cane flute (pito) and the shaker card for the chinchines.",
  "recipe": "classic early-2010s parachicos, carnival Processional. flute like credited flute shaker source unspecified, acoustic membrane drum. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
